<p>Do not add these. Annual revenue, capital raised, and a ten-year forecast are different kinds of quantity, and the forecast is not $1.8 trillion "at risk" in any accounting sense.</p>
<p>The SIA breakdown is where the useful detail is. Of the $303 billion, $165.2 billion is ground equipment, and $125.8 billion of that is GNSS equipment: the navigation chips in phones, cars, ships and farm machinery. Satellite services, which includes broadband and TV, are $105 billion. Remote sensing, the business ICEYE is in, is $3.6 billion. Launch is $12.4 billion. Everything filed under space sustainability, which covers servicing, life extension, situational awareness and debris removal, comes to about $500 million.</p>
