        <section id="what-to-watch">
          <h2>9. What to watch</h2>
<p>Integrity ISR expects two of Cosmos 2612's sister satellites, 2611 and 2613, to cross the orbital plane of another ICEYE satellite, X37, around 6 November and 15 November. If either one repeats the climb-and-descend sequence that 2612 used, it will show up in public tracking data a week or two before the closest approach.</p>
<p>Langbroek posts his analysis at <a href="https://sattrackcam.blogspot.com/">SatTrackCam Leiden</a>. LeoLabs publishes its tracking commentary on its own site and through reporters. ICEYE has not said whether X36 is healthy. That is the next fact worth having, and we will update this piece when someone states it on the record.</p>
        </section>

